Z||000013||firstfiero||05-03-2001||10:22 AM||||     Don't care if it got beat or not...I'd much rather drive the 928 over any wagon. I don't care whats under the hood....it's a station wagon. The 70s version of a mini van.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Not to start a flame war but I don't get it...suping a wagon is like suping up a civic whats the point? sorry just my oppinion...I got to admit though it is one hell of a sleeper!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">  <BR>Todd <BR>  86se<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/toddsfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||05-03-2001||11:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>     ...suping a wagon is like suping up a civic whats the point? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think it's a cool idea. <BR>I've seen pics of a modded/slammed Impala wagon with "Bonneville disk" wheel covers. <BR>Looked absolutely wicked. I'd drive it any time!<BR>What's the point? <BR>1. You have a good old (or new) American V-8.<BR>2. It's a HELL of a sleeper.<BR>3. You can take many of your friends with you.<BR>4. You have room for Fiero parts.<BR>5. You have room to transport stuff for other projects, too.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||6
