Z||000016||Cameron||05-03-2001||07:55 PM||||Well I guess that's true about wagons and people not wanting to race them...but me I'll give anybody a race that wants one even when I was driving my '01 Jeep Wrangler Sahara with a 3.73 axle ratio and a 5 speed manual (instead of the 3 speed auto).  I never won...but always had fun.  It's not always winning that matters, its how you get there.  But I do admit, I show respect to the Vipers, Vettes, and Cobras around here, because that's the least they deserve.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||JohnnyK||05-03-2001||08:36 PM||||Too many problems in a 928? HAHAHAQHAHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAHAHHAHAHAHAHAH. Dude, You we own, FIEROS!!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||05-03-2001||09:15 PM||||I have owned my car for 5 years now , summer driven only , put in one clutch , one waterpump...<P>Autocrossed and done track events since the day I got it , driven the hell out of it. the above problems are the only ones I have had. <P>Lets take a 928 for example , I'm somewhat of a porsche-phile and I know a wee bit about them. Like how the waterpump tends to corrode on the bottom leaking out fluid , this water pump replacement is worth about $1200 US dollars. While you replace it get the timing chain done as well (+$700) . Simply changing the plugs on a 3.6ltr twin plug flat 6 can cost you $130. We just had our cars(94 911 3.8) tuned up , valves adjusted , belts changed , filters changed , ect. this was the usual service , nothing out of the ordinary , $1960 later the car is all tuned up , This was a typical porsche service (thats canadian dollars)<P>I haven't had any major problems with my fiero for the abuse I have placed upon it. I think there is a great misconception by some people that fiero's are not reliable. I got my car when I was 18 , ran track events , boiled brake fluid , you name it. The car has been driven 10/10ths at every event , by not only me but other people. It has only left me stranded once when the clutch blew.<P>No doubt a porsche is a reliable car. Ours is a marvel of technology and thus you pay for it when it comes time to service. and you don't want to get a half assed service job done on the car , it will only cost you more in the end. I know of a few 928's , s4's and such that are maintenance nightmares. th 928 in the porsche community is kinda regaurded as a quirky car , get a car with low miles that has had service done religously and your fine , get a car with a bit of wear and your in for it.<P>The rule of thumb is , always go to buy any used porsche with an extra $5000 to spend on maintenance. (higher end cars) chain tensioners on earlier cars , magnesium blocks that pull head studs..there are tons of little quirks you have to know , espically on a 928.<P><BR>Just my experience with Porsche's I know more on 911's than any other porsche , I have had some seat time in 928's and had lots of friends that race them. <P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000019||firstfiero||05-04-2001||02:37 PM||||   You are absolutley right about porsches. I had a 924. Their considered the cheapest porsche to own and maintain. The last part I bought was 400 bucks for a damn wind shield wiper motor. What I like about my fiero is cheap fun.That is a sweet 911 by the way. <BR>   Let me also say I'm inpressed...I stated an oppionion and didn't get flamed for it. That's  a nice change!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">      <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||1
